From: ohmail
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:40:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] tests: departed objects and departed peers leave the
 bridge

Two in-process tests that read the bridge's own state, with the bridge on a
private bus (GTestDBus) that serves as the accessibility bus.

cache-departed: an object queued for the cache that goes defunct before the
queue drains is cached again from the queue; once it is finalized it must be
gone from the cache, and Cache.GetItems must answer with live objects only.
Red on 2.52.0, where the re-added entry outlives its object and GetItems refs
freed memory (the class of at-spi2-core #178).

direct-connection, second case: peers that open the application's p2p address,
make one call and close must not stay in direct_connections. libdbus 1.14
keeps no pidfd per peer, so the upstream case skips there; this one counts the
connections the bridge holds.

[ohmail: not upstream; carried with the backports above.]
